 "result": "Three failing tests are not caused by the `partitioned` / `set_cookie` problem.\n\n1. **`tests/test_request.py::test_limit_config`**\n   - It asserts `r.max_form_memory_size == 500_000` but gets `None`.\n   - The installed Werkzeug 3.0.3 `Request` has no such attribute. It was added in 3.1, so this is the same underlying cause (Werkzeug older than the required `>=3.1.0`), but it is a different missing feature and not the `set_cookie` error.\n\n2. **`tests/test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view`**\n   - It fails with `RuntimeError: Install Tessel with the 'async' extra in order to use async views.`, raised at `src/tessel/app.py:1096`.\n   - `asgiref` isn't installed (`import asgiref` raises `ModuleNotFoundError`). This is a missing optional dependency, unrelated to Werkzeug.\n\n3. **`tests/test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]`**\n   - I never captured its traceback. It failed in my first full run, but it passes in isolation and I couldn't reproduce it afterwards.\n   - It is probably collateral damage from the `AppContext` leaked by `test_stream_keeps_session`, which would trace back to the main cause indirectly. That is unconfirmed.\n\nThe teardown **error** on `test_stream_keeps_session` (`assert not leaks`, `tests/conftest.py:79`) is a consequence of the main cause, not a separate one.",
